}
```
So `.reaction` contains an avatar (`.reaction__avatar`) and a span with text (`.txt-small.txt-medium` maybe). The `.btn` inside is the delete button (small font).

```
.reaction--deleteable { cursor: pointer; hover brightness... }
```
Applied when the reaction belongs to Current.user (deleteable).

```
.reaction__avatar, .reaction__avatar .avatar, .reaction__form-label, .reaction form { block-size: 100%; }
```

```
.reaction__delete { display: none; .expanded & { display: grid; } }
```
So `.reaction__delete` is hidden; when an ancestor has `.expanded`, shown. This is the delete control inside your own reaction. So clicking your reaction toggles `.expanded` on the `.reaction` (or ancestor), revealing `.reaction__delete`.

```
.reaction__form {
  transition: none;
